# 10-Role Orchestration Rule

Use this operating model for implementation-heavy requests in this repository.

**User U16:** Two lanes — see `.cursor/rules/team-execution-vs-governance.mdc`.

## Team Topology

### Execution lane (delivery)
- 3 Dev: BE Lead (API+DB+technical direction), FE, Mobile.
- 1 QA Lead: test strategy, automation, defect lifecycle, evidence.

### Governance lane (supervise → discuss → update Cursor)
- 1 PM: delivery ownership, dispatch, bus, WBS.
- 1 SA: architecture drift, ADR, NFR boundaries.
- 2 BA: process + data traceability, spec_gap deltas.
- 1 TA: Technical Auditor = TM (technical governance) + QC (Go/No-Go).

## Coordination Protocol
- Never let agents coordinate by ad-hoc chat only.
- Use shared project artifacts as source of truth.
- Required updates per cycle:
  - execution board
  - daily sync
  - decisions log
  - defect register (if defects exist)
  - traceability matrix

## Execution Loop
1. Read current backlog/board and pick top priorities.
2. **Dispatch Dev + QA** (execution); governance roles only on trigger or post-wave review.
3. Integrate and validate (build/test/simulation evidence).
4. **Governance cycle:** PM/SA/BA/TA review → discuss → update rules/skills/KB/hooks (`GOVERNANCE_IMPROVEMENT_LOOP.md`).
5. Repeat until all in-scope use cases are DONE.

## Quality Gates
- No merge-ready claim without build/test/simulation evidence.
- No use case marked DONE without traceability completion.
- Keep deterministic error behavior and strict validation in new APIs.
